{"ts": "2026-08-17T10:24:11Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 105, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "1\t# Design: Edit a task title\n2\t\n3\tTaiga #2 \u00b7 consumes `docs/spec.md`\n4\t\n5\t## Conventions established (before designing anything)\n6\t\n7\t- No component library, no icon set, no design tokens file \u2014 plain CSS in\n8\t  `frontend/src/App.css`, function components, hooks only.\n9\t- Existing button style is a single neutral style (`button { border, white\n10\t  bg, radius 5px }`) with no primary/secondary visual hierarchy \u2014 Done and\n11\t  Delete look the same. Nothing today distinguishes \"safe\" vs \"destructive\"\n12\t  by color.\n13\t- Existing form pattern is `AddTask.jsx`: a `<form onSubmit>` wrapping an\n14\t  `<input>` + submit `<button>`, client-side `.trim()` check before calling\n15\t  the handler, `aria-label` on the input.\n16\t- Existing per-row actions (`TaskList.jsx`) are plain-text buttons with an\n17\t  `aria-label` that includes the task's title (`` `Complete ${task.title}` ``)\n18\t  for screen-reader disambiguation between rows.\n19\t- Existing error surface is a single global banner in `App.jsx` \u2014\n20\t  `<p className=\"error\" role=\"alert\">` \u2014 fed by `run()`'s catch block.\n21\t- Existing color tokens in use: text `#16191c`, border `#ccd2d6`, error text\n22\t  `#a3271d` on error bg `#fbe9e7`, muted `#6b7780`, card bg `#fff`, page bg\n23\t  `#f6f7f8`.\n24\t\n25\t**Decision: introduce no new component, no new color, no new button style.**\n26\tEverything below extends `TaskList.jsx` and `App.css` in place, per the\n27\tspec's affected areas.\n28\t\n29\t## Interaction model\n30\t", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_011JMLDcpeA55U7cMZgGvsrC", "session_id": "3828aad9-a333-4ced-8ef5-81593968620a"}}
