{"ts": "2026-08-17T10:24:37Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 117, "kind": "tool_use", "text": "Write", "meta": {"native_type": "assistant", "block_type": "tool_use", "tool_use_id": "toolu_015En8W5nbvMQEMWFsK7U8CC", "input": {"file_path": "/home/dev/projects/test-project/docs/implementation.md", "content": "# Implementation: Edit a task title\n\nTaiga #2 \u00b7 implements `docs/spec.md` + `docs/design.md`\n\n## What changed, by file\n\n- **`backend/app/store.py`** \u2014 `TaskStore.set_title(task_id, title)`: looks up\n  the task, returns `None` if missing (mirrors `set_done`'s existing\n  not-found pattern), else sets `.title` and returns the task.\n- **`backend/app/main.py`** \u2014 `PATCH /api/tasks/{task_id}`, reusing the\n  existing `TaskIn` model so an empty/oversized title 422s before the\n  handler runs. 404s via `HTTPException` if `set_title` returns `None`.\n- **`frontend/src/api.js`** \u2014 `updateTask(id, title)`, same `request()`\n  wrapper as the other calls.\n- **`frontend/src/App.jsx`** \u2014 wires `onEdit` through the existing `run()`\n  error-handling wrapper, same shape as `onComplete`/`onDelete`.\n- **`frontend/src/components/TaskList.jsx`** \u2014 per-row edit mode: `Edit`\n  button (between `Done` and `Delete`) swaps the row's title span + actions\n  for a `<form>` with an autofocused input and Save/Cancel buttons. Client-side\n  trim-check blocks empty saves before any request, mirroring `AddTask.jsx`.\n  `Escape` and `Cancel` both revert with no request sent. Only one row can be\n  in edit mode at a time (starting a new edit discards any unsaved draft).\n- **`frontend/src/App.css`** \u2014 styles for the edit form/input/error message,\n  reusing existing color tokens only.\n- **`backend/tests/test_tasks.py`** \u2014 success/404/422 cases for `PATCH`.\n- **`e2e/test_tasks_e2e.py`** \u2014 real-browser coverage for AC1-5 and both\n  open-question defaults (done tasks stay editable; single-task edit mode).\n\n## Fix-cycle addendum (attempt 2)\n\nThe test stage found a real defect via a live browser test: the edit\ninput and the always-present `AddTask` input both had\n`aria-label=\"Task title\"`, so as soon as any row entered edit mode two\ninputs shared one accessible name. `docs/design.md`'s reasoning about\n`aria-label` collisions only considered row-vs-row, not row-vs-AddTask.\n\nRoot-cause fix: `frontend/src/components/TaskList.jsx`'s edit input now\nuses `aria-label={\\`Edit title for ${task.title}\\`}` \u2014 same per-row-title\npattern already used by the Save/Cancel/Complete/Edit/Delete buttons next to\nit, so it's both unique and consistent with the rest of the row.\n\nUpdated `e2e/test_tasks_e2e.py`:\n- `edit_input()` now locates by `Edit title for {title}` instead of the\n  ambiguous shared label (still scoped to `ul.task-list` as a second layer\n  of disambiguation).\n- The test that documented the collision as a known defect\n  (`test_edit_input_shares_the_add_tasks_accessible_name`) is now\n  `test_edit_input_has_a_distinct_accessible_name`, asserting `\"Task title\"`\n  resolves to exactly one element (AddTask's) and `\"Edit title for buy milk\"`\n  resolves to exactly one element (the edit input) while a row is in edit mode.\n\nVerified in this session:\n- `python3 -m pytest backend/tests e2e/ -q` \u2192 42/42 pass\n- `cd frontend && npm run build` \u2192 clean\n\n## Known limitations / follow-ups (unchanged from review, not addressed here)\n\n- `frontend/src/api.js`'s `request()` renders FastAPI's 422 `detail` (a list\n  of validation-error objects) as `\"[object Object]\"` in the error banner for\n  the oversized-title case (AC5). Pre-existing, shared with `AddTask`'s\n  create path, out of scope per `docs/design.md:64-71`.\n- No frontend unit-test framework is installed (`frontend/package.json` has\n  no `test` script despite `CLAUDE.md` documenting `npm test`); AC1-5\n  coverage lives in the Playwright e2e suite instead.\n- `backend/tests/_scratch_check_422.py` is a leftover untracked scratch file\n  from the test stage's manual 422-shape inspection. It is **not** part of\n  this implementation and should be deleted before commit; this session's\n  sandbox permissions block `rm`/`git clean` on it (same restriction the\n  test stage hit), so it's still present in the working tree.\n\n## How to verify\n\n```bash\ncd backend  && python3 -m pytest -q\npython3 -m pytest backend/tests e2e/ -q   # from repo root, real Chromium e2e\ncd frontend && npm run build\n```\n"}, "session_id": "3828aad9-a333-4ced-8ef5-81593968620a"}}
